t to skate a stand an  organization that works to bring skating  to Cambodia Afghanistan and South Africa  in 2015  Hawk told ABC 10 News skateboarding is  empowering women in Afghanistan more  than probably any other sport to me  honestly  in 2007 Hawk helped found athletes for  Hope which fosters connections between  the world of elite sports and young  hopefuls more than 10 years later  they're still going strong Hawk has been  a hot commodity in the entertainment  world for decades over the years he's  played himself on The Simpsons appeared  in kiddie fare like rocket power and  taken bit roles and action flicks like  deck dogs oh and don't forget his cameo  in the 2005 film Lords of Dogtown where  he played an astronaut who wipes out on  his skateboard  more recently Hawk popped up on the  popular YouTube hit Epic Meal Time and  he even made an appearance on Sesame  Street back in 2008 skateboard for  wheels on a skateboard morning also we  would be remiss not to mention his star  turn in the Aquabats Super Show  what was it like being thrown in outer  space we were in outer space skate  culture has been influencing the fashion  world for a long time from Avril  Lavigne's stylings in the early 2000s to  the classic vans off-the-wall sneakers  skating and fashion have always seemed  to go hand in hand it was only a matter  of time before an actual skater took  that relationship to the next level Tony  Hawk did this with the Tony Hawk  signature line a collection he debuted  at Paris Fashion Week the line is an  upscale take on skater style as  envisioned by one of skating subcultures  most legendary heroes talking to Vogue  Hawk weighed in on the success of street  wear brands like palace and supreme  noting how they're being recognized and  embraced by a much bigger crowd people  who want to have that look but who don't  necessarily skate in 2019  he told heist nabiyya t if we reach that  level I want to join into because I feel  like I have enough to offer an